Specification String Calculator

# In the configuration, set tags to NOT $TBD 
# Then untag each calculation one by one and make each pass 

Attributes CalculationCases
| Name   | DataType |
| Input  | String   |
| Result | String   |

$TBD
Calculation Empty String Returns Zero
Description Returns zero when no numbers are supplied.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input | Result |
|       | 0      |

$TBD
Calculation Single Number Returns Value
Description Returns the number when a single number is supplied.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input | Result |
| 1     | 1      |
| 42    | 42     |

$TBD
Calculation Multiple Numbers Are Summed
Description Returns the sum of all comma-separated numbers.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input    | Result |
| 1,2      | 3      |
| 1,2,3    | 6      |
| 10,20,30 | 60     |

$TBD
Calculation Newlines Are Valid Separators
Description Treats newlines the same as commas when separating numbers.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input  | Result |
| 1\n2   | 3      |
| 1\n2,3 | 6      |

$TBD
Calculation Custom Delimiter Is Supported
Description Uses the delimiter specified at the start of the input.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input    | Result |
| //;\n1;2 | 3      |
| //       | 0      |

$TBD
Calculation Negative Numbers Cause Error
Description Reports the negative numbers that were supplied.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input | Result |
| -1    | Error  |
| 1,-2  | Error  |
| -1,-2 | Error  |

$TBD
Calculation Numbers Greater Than One Thousand Are Ignored
Description Excludes numbers greater than one thousand from the sum.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input  | Result |
| 2,1001 | 2      |
| 1000,2 | 1002   |
| 1001,2 | 2      |

$TBD
Calculation Delimiters Of Any Length Are Supported
Description Allows a custom delimiter containing multiple characters.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input          | Result |
| //[***]\n1***2 | 3      |
| //[--]\n2--3   | 5      |

$TBD
Calculation Multiple Delimiters Are Supported
Description Allows more than one custom delimiter.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input           | Result |
| //[*][%]\n1*2%3 | 6      |
| //[#][@]\n2#3@4 | 9      |

$TBD
Calculation Multiple Long Delimiters Are Supported
Description Allows multiple delimiters of arbitrary length.
Examples: CalculationCases
| Input                   | Result |
| //[***][%%]\n1***2%%3   | 6      |
| //[abc][xyz]\n4abc5xyz6 | 15     |